## a debian:13 container as the off-box machine: restic alone
$ apt-get update && apt-get install -y restic
restic 0.18.0 compiled with go1.24.4 on linux/arm64
files in /etc/ssl/certs: 0
dpkg-query: package 'ca-certificates' is not installed and no information is available
$ restic -r rest:https://example.com/ cat config   (any https storage; stopped after 20 s of its retrying)
SFatal: unable to open config file: Head "https://:***@example.com/config": tls: failed to verify certificate: x509: certificate signed by unknown authority
Is there a repository at the following location?
rest:https://example.com/
[exit 0]
$ apt-get install -y restic ca-certificates
Status: install ok installed
Fatal: repository does not exist: unable to open config file: <config/> does not exist
Is there a repository at the following location?
rest:https://example.com/
[exit 0]
## backblaze-b2 and rclone, Debian 13
b2 command line tool, version 3.19.1
rclone v1.60.1-DEV
no b2 on PATH: the program is backblaze-b2
backblaze-b2 create-key [-h] [--bucket BUCKET] [--name-prefix NAME_PREFIX]
                        [--duration DURATION] [--all-capabilities]
                        keyName [capabilities]

backblaze-b2 authorize-account [-h] [applicationKeyId] [applicationKey]

Prompts for Backblaze applicationKeyId and applicationKey (unless they are given
on the command line).

backblaze-b2 ls [-h] [--long] [--json] [--replication] [--versions] [-r]
                [--with-wildcard] [--include FILTERS] [--exclude FILTERS]
                [bucketName] [folderName]

backblaze-b2 delete-key [-h] applicationKeyId

Deletes the specified application key by its ID.
backblaze-b2 clear-account [-h]

Erases everything in local cache.
[--replication] [--versions] [-r]
                [--with-wildcard] [--include FILTERS] [--exclude FILTERS]
                [bucketName] [folderName]

backblaze-b2 delete-key [-h] applicationKeyId

Deletes the specified application key by its ID.
backblaze-b2 clear-account [-h]

Erases everything in local cache.
